# Koishi plugin

- Export a normal Koishi **Plugin**. Do not `extend Adapter` / `extend Bot` for dynamic-bot.
- Use adapters already in the Koishi instance (`ctx.bots`, `bot.sendMessage`, `h()`), including `adapter-onebot`. Do not implement OneBot or platform Adapters here.
- Translate **generated** proto types ↔ `h()` / `session` only. Do not define parallel TS interfaces for DBK messages.
- On `message.send`, resolve image / video / audio URIs to bytes then `h.image` / `h.video` / `h.audio`(data, mime). Decode `data:` and `base64://` locally; fetch other URIs with `ctx.http.file`. Do not pass those URLs through to adapters (Discord / Telegram cannot fetch dynamic-bot localhost). Resolve failure fails that unit; do not silently drop the segment or fall back to the URL.
- On `message` events: emit `message.created`; drop the bot’s own messages; **do not** parse commands or reply with `session.send`.
- Implement `bots.list`, `targets.list`, `targets.get`, `message.send`, `message.recall`.
- Map `bot.status` to DBK `READY` / `CONNECTING` / `UNAVAILABLE`. Do not use `bot.isActive` (CONNECT/RECONNECT are active but not ready).
- Declare `features` per bot (`message.recall`, `targets.list`, `target.user` / `target.group` / `target.channel` / `target.thread`, …). Detect TargetKind from bot methods (`getChannelList` vs flat `getGuildList`), not from `bot.platform` names. Do not pretend a bot can list all chats when it has no nested `channel.list`.
- Platform tokens and OneBot WS stay in Koishi adapter config, not in dynamic-bot.
- Do not hardcode `GATEWAY_VERSION`. In this repo it is `git describe`; published npm falls back to `package.json`.
